  "coverage": [
    "Immutable checkpoint provenance isolates copied snapshots. Preparation returns independent plans and hashes actual stored bytes; failed preparation, SQL errors, deferred commit failure and allocation failure do not publish speculative snapshot state.",
    "Nested transcript operations use an operation savepoint. Accepted original and written fingerprints distinguish external commit from rollback across revisions, appends, removals, replacements and blob materialization; next writes are tested before reload.",
    "Mutable write overloads publish canonical messages and IDs alongside SQL outcomes. Const compatibility adapters use private copies. IDs are assigned from tool-aware, filesystem-independent normalization at actual positions before archive projection; existing IDs and provider associations are retained.",
    "Legacy blob and row layouts project checkpoint references read-only. First successful blob writes verify the raw source and materialize canonical rows and portable references transactionally.",
    "Reconciliation prepares from coherent transcript and journal reads, then verifies exact inputs before publication. Archive preparation permits unrelated writers to commit. Tool completion shares one prepared canonical result between journal and transcript; historical read_file content keeps its own normalization policy during blob conversion.",
    "Prepared publication merges pending normalization and requested revision into one update, reuses statements and serialized payloads, and releases pending payloads after owning commit. Ordinary appends reuse compact provenance, perform zero acknowledged checkpoint-row reads and preserve suffix-only provider serialization.",
    "Post-commit publication and retired JSON cleanup are nonallocating. Cleanup workspace is reserved before commit to avoid the JSON library allocating during container destruction. Existing response rollback, private receipts, cancellation and provider-error tests remain passing.",
    "Repair backup diagnostics use the injected filesystem, including backups invisible to native filesystem queries. A failed verification preserves the original failure and marks the candidate location publication-unconfirmed.",
    "Narrow Semgrep fixtures reject speculative provenance mutation and public preparing writes from reconciliation/tool completion. Runtime fault and filesystem instrumentation remain authoritative.",
    "Full offline host, sanitizer and Linux suites, twenty shuffled fault-suite repetitions, all three analyzers and detection/runner tests, pinned Semgrep, benchmarks and Tiger cross-build/static checks distinguish executed tests from unexecuted hardware verification.",
    "Schema 7, strict archive trust, lazy anchor pinning, both serialized cache limits, capture quotas, database-wide repair invalidation and exactly two preparation attempts remain unchanged."
  ],
  "excluded": [
    "Eager artifact anchor pinning",
